# Built binaries (not checked in). The farcast CLI builds to ./farcast; the
# Planck harness is run via `go run` (see docs/runbooks/phase-1-validation.md).
/farcast

# Module harness binaries, if built into the package dir. (Don't ignore a bare
# "planck"/"fatline"/"shrike" — those are source directories; only the binary at
# these paths, e.g. from `go build -o fatline ./fatline/cmd/fatline`.)
/planck/planck
/fatline/fatline
/shrike/shrike

# The Phase 2 validation runbook builds farcast/fatline/shrike into ./bin/.
/bin/

# One-off local build artifacts (e.g. from validation runs).
/x_farcast
/x_planck

# Local-only operator context. HANDOVER.md carries the live GCP project, the
# cluster's DNS endpoint, the service-account key path, and account emails;
# .claude/ is this machine's agent settings. Neither belongs in a public repo,
# and neither has ever been tracked — this makes that survive a `git add -A`.
/HANDOVER.md
/.claude/

# The Apple client's build output: SwiftPM's .build/ and .swiftpm/, the
# DerivedData ./check.sh points xcodebuild at, and Xcode's per-user state.
/farsight/client/apple/.build/
/farsight/client/apple/FarSightKit/.build/
/farsight/client/apple/FarSightKit/.swiftpm/
xcuserdata/

# The layers and digest table a release build embeds in farcast (ADR 0023
# decision 4). farcast-release supplies them with go build -overlay from its
# -out directory; they are never written here and never committed.
/farsight/cli/internal/components/layers/
